/* The <%= human_name.downcase %> block's public styles. Every colour is a --th- token:
   a built-in's token values are written in tokens.css, light and dark, and
   declared in the type's `tokens` (block types spec, decision 3). A block's
   token is defined from the theme's base tokens (var(--th-ink),
   color-mix() of --th-accent and --th-surface, ...) wherever one is right,
   so a theme that re-colours its base re-colours the block, and holds a
   literal only where no base token is.
   Written by bin/rails generate block_type: while this line stands, bin/rails
   destroy block_type <%= file_name %> removes this file. Take it out once the
   stylesheet is yours. */
.content-block--<%= file_name %> {
}
